  "details": "<p><em>The Barrington Atlas Directory</em> notes: Mandra di Mezzo, rural sanctuary?. Writing in BTCGI, Falzone reports that a Greek inscription was found at the locality known as Mandra di Mezzo. This place is located in a place known now as Poggioreale. Falsone does not report the date of the find, but presumably it occurred prior to 1959. The inscription uses the Greek alphabet of Selinunte and is dated to the sixth century BCE.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
